    "body": "## Chat05A server-authorized vote atom\n\n- Added an operator-only person registry with idempotent registration and immutable battle-to-person bindings for both participants.\n- Added individual spectator bearer capabilities. Operator-only routes issue, rotate and revoke them by expected generation. D1 stores only SHA-256 digests, tracks generations and records digest history. Capabilities are returned once to the trusted operator; no invitations are sent.\n- Participant personIds cannot receive spectator capabilities or cast ballots. The vote API accepts only `choice` and derives personId from the active spectator bearer digest. D1 rechecks capability generation when inserting.\n- A revealed DRAW creates the stable `deriveSocialVoteId(battleId)` in the same D1 batch as the reveal transition, only when both trusted participant bindings exist. Legacy/unbound battles still reveal but cannot open votes.\n- Database constraints enforce one vote per battle and one immutable ballot per (voteId, personId). Same-choice retries return the stored ballot; changed-choice retries conflict.\n- `nextTextOrigin` defaults to unknown. Only explicit server-owned `authored` provenance can trigger the text contract. This Worker has no authoritative server-owned text source, so authored-text vote creation is not wired.\n\n## Validation on exact HEAD\n\nHEAD: `463d75ae9181fae886ae9e198698219f95106993`  \nBase: `main@b435e70eb88b87b3c3324ef2a2da14cdf473f229`\n\n- GitHub Actions: `private-api-local`, `sqlite-cas`, `wrangler-local-d1`, and `capture` all completed successfully on this SHA, including both duplicate check runs.\n- Local workerd/D1 integration verifies participant exclusion, forged personId rejection, hash-only capability storage, revocation and reissue, repeat and changed ballot requests, concurrent ballots, stable vote creation, and legacy DRAW reveal.\n- The D1 integration stops and restarts the Worker with the same persist directory, then verifies the existing voteId and ballot survive.\n- Local Node contract and harness checks: 24/24 passed.\n- Independent `critical_reviewer`: `PASS_STATIC_SECURITY_AND_RESTART_TEST_REVIEW` on this SHA.\n\n## Boundary\n\nThis remains a Draft PR and is not overall Chat05A PASS or hosted/runtime acceptance. Authored-text vote creation still needs an authoritative server-owned text path. No merge, deploy, Cloudflare operation, real invitation, Chat05B, NPC, timer, economy, or UI change is included.\n\n",
